document.write('<li class="rss-item"><a class="rss-item" href="http://feeds.cellphones.ca/~r/cellphonesetc/~3/2Uz6t2hD8lE/" target="_blank">HTC Thunderbolt 4G (aka Incredible HD) specs revealed</a><br />');
document.write('<p>Here?s some juicy info on the rumored upcoming HTC Thunderbolt 4G aka Incredible HD. </p> <p><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/HTC-Thunderbolt-4G.jpg\"><img src=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/HTC-Thunderbolt-4G.jpg\" alt=\"HTC Thunderbolt 4G\" title=\"HTC Thunderbolt 4G\" width=\"560\" height=\"274\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-21093\" /></a></p> <p><a href=\"http://www.htcinside.de/htc/geruechte/exklusiv-das-htc-thunderbolt-4g-taucht-zum-ersten-mal-im-warensystem-eines-deutschen-elektrofachmarktes-auf.html\">HTCInside</a> has leaked its purported specs which include a 4.3-inch touchscreen display, 8-megapixel rear camera with dual LED flash, 5-megapixel front-facing camera, 1.2GHz processor, WiFi, Bluetooth, GPS, 16GB internal memory complemented by a microSD card slot for additional storage, Android 2.3 OS, and most interesting of all, quad-band UMTS, LTE, HSDPA, HSUPA connectivity. Meaning, this isn?t the <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/cell-plans/carriers/verizon/\">Verizon</a>-exclusive handset that?s been hitting the headlines as of late, and is actually a GSM variant headed for Europe, which could potentially find its way to the local market as well. </p> <p>Excited? We sure are. Of course, all this is yet to be verified so treat this new tidbit with a healthy grain of salt until further evidence surfaces to support it. </p> <p>[<a href=\"http://www.bgr.com/2010/12/31/rumor-specifications-for-htcs-thunderbolt-4g-emerge/\">source</a>]</p> <p>This is a post from <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/\">Cell Phones Etc.</a> entitled:<br /><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0021091/\">HTC Thunderbolt 4G (aka Incredible HD) specs revealed</a></p><img src=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/cellphonesetc/~4/2Uz6t2hD8lE\" height=\"1\" width=\"1\"/>');
