document.write('<li class="rss-item"><a class="rss-item" href="http://feeds.cellphones.ca/~r/cellphonesetc/~3/JRtgsOh_570/" target="_blank">Mobile Phone Charging via microUSB in Europe begins in 2011</a><br />');
document.write('<p>A standardized mobile phone charging port is finally coming, not yet in our neck of the woods though but in Europe. </p> <p><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/No-to-different-charging-ports.jpg\"><img src=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/No-to-different-charging-ports.jpg\" alt=\"No to different charging ports\" title=\"No to different charging ports\" width=\"225\" height=\"200\" class=\"alignleft size-medium wp-image-21083\" /></a>This initiative was <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post007907/\">first put forward</a> back in June 2009, but it?s only now that it will take effect. MicroUSB is the interface that?s been approved, and beginning next year, all new phones to be released in Europe will have this as its charging port. Big names in the industry such as Nokia, Sony Ericsson, LG, Motorola, Samsung, and Apple all have signed up to be part of this noble cause. You can read more about this landmark decision over <a href=\"http://ec.europa.eu/enterprise/sectors/rtte/chargers/index_en.htm\">here</a>. </p> <p>The big question on our mind is, what will happen to the iPhone? It?s easy for other manufacturers to adapt to this new rule since they release a number of phone models every year, but in the case of Apple, they only have one model and it uses a 20-pin interface which also doubles as a sync port and is standard on their all their iOS devices. Will Apple change this to adapt to the new standard in Europe, or will they just provide a microUSB adaptor instead? My guess is it?s the latter, but only time will tell. </p> <p>More importantly though, now that its taking effect, we?re hoping other countries will follow the EU&#8217;s lead and adapt this new standardized micrUSB charging port.</p> <p>[<a href=\"http://www.gsmarena.com/microusb_to_become_the_standard_charger_plug_in_the_eu_next_year-news-2181.php\">source</a>]</p> <p>This is a post from <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/\">Cell Phones Etc.</a> entitled:<br /><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0021081/\">Mobile Phone Charging via microUSB in Europe begins in 2011</a></p><img src=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/cellphonesetc/~4/JRtgsOh_570\" height=\"1\" width=\"1\"/>');
document.write('</li>');
document.write('<li class="rss-item"><a class="rss-item" href="http://feeds.cellphones.ca/~r/cellphonesetc/~3/76cO9-naIRg/" target="_blank">Bloomberg Businessweek: Verizon iPhone could be launched on Valentine?s Day</a><br />');
document.write('<p><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/06/Verizon-iPhone.png\"><img src=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/06/Verizon-iPhone.png\" alt=\"Verizon iPhone\" title=\"Verizon iPhone\" width=\"162\" height=\"180\" class=\"alignleft size-medium wp-image-16059\" /></a>Back in <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0016057/\">June</a>, Bloomberg talked about the much-rumored Verizon iPhone debuting in January of next year. There?s still no new evidence to support this even though it?s only a few weeks away. What we do have though is a new prediction, this time coming from <a href=\"http://www.businessweek.com/magazine/content/11_02/b4210034485538.htm\">Bloomberg Businessweek</a>. According to their report, Apple will ?<em>likely host one of its splashy product introductions to announce a new version of the iPhone that works on Verizon?s network</em>? possibly on Valentine?s day. </p> <p>How much truer is this from previous Verizon iPhone rumors? We?re not holding our breathe on this new one, but it does line up nicely with all the talk we?ve heard in the past that a CDMA iPhone will be released in 2011. </p> <p>Of course, taking a look at the big picture, this is still no guarantee of it happening. Talk of a <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post006142/\">CDMA iPhone</a> talk has been around since 2009 wherein they estimated it would be launched in 2010. Did it happen? No, so why should we be more excited with this latest one when, just like before, there?s still hard evidence to support this? </p> <p>With that being said, this doesn?t mean we?ve given up hope that this is true. We?re hoping. It?s just that we?re not betting our money on it. </p> <p>[<a href=\"http://www.bgr.com/2010/12/30/businessweek-verizon-iphone-to-be-announced-by-valentines-day/\">source</a>]</p> <p>This is a post from <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/\">Cell Phones Etc.</a> entitled:<br /><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0021073/\">Bloomberg Businessweek: Verizon iPhone could be launched on Valentine&#8217;s Day</a></p><img src=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/cellphonesetc/~4/76cO9-naIRg\" height=\"1\" width=\"1\"/>');
document.write('</li>');
document.write('<li class="rss-item"><a class="rss-item" href="http://feeds.cellphones.ca/~r/cellphonesetc/~3/NsgtmDkrFqg/" target="_blank">CNN: iPhone 4 ?Antennagate? tops biggest tech ?fails? of 2010</a><br />');
document.write('<p>It may already be water under the bridge, but the whole issue concerning the iPhone 4?s signal reception woes has just become the main reason why <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/cell-phones/manufacturers/apple/\">Apple</a> &#8211; or more specifically the iPhone 4 &#8211; landed at the top spot of <a href=\"http://edition.cnn.com/2010/TECH/innovation/12/28/tech.fails.year/index.html\">CNN?s biggest tech ?fails? for 2010</a>. </p> <p><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/06/iPhone-4.jpg\"><img src=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/06/iPhone-4-219x300.jpg\" alt=\"iPhone 4\" title=\"iPhone 4\" width=\"219\" height=\"300\" class=\"alignleft size-medium wp-image-15462\" /></a>While Apple did a very good job in reinventing the iPhone and sprucing it up with new treats, the ?antennagate? controversy, unfortunately, became more of the focal point after the <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/cell-phones/apple-iphone-4/\">iPhone 4</a> rolled out to the public. It was negative publicity, but publicity nonetheless. As such, this is also one of reasos the iPhone 4 topped another year-ending countdown, the one of <a href=\"http://yearinreview.yahoo.com/2010/us_10_obsessions\">Yahoo rounding up the top 10 obsessions of 2010</a>. </p> <p>Apple issued an official statement citing a <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0016158/\">faulty firmware</a> as the culprit, but later on <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0016508/\">offered free bumpers/cases</a> to interested customers which basically contradicts their explanation that it?s software-related. </p> <p>The ?antennagate? issue eventually died down, and as their <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0019186/\">sales</a> will prove, it hardly affected the latest iPhone?s popularity across the globe. Sure, it would have been better if it never really happened, but for better or worse, it surely helped Apple and the iPhone 4 still be one of the hottest topics even as we bid 2010 goodbye. </p> <p>This is a post from <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/\">Cell Phones Etc.</a> entitled:<br /><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0021068/\">CNN: iPhone 4 &#8216;Antennagate&#8217; tops biggest tech &#8216;fails&#8217; of 2010</a></p><img src=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/cellphonesetc/~4/NsgtmDkrFqg\" height=\"1\" width=\"1\"/>');
document.write('</li>');
document.write('<li class="rss-item"><a class="rss-item" href="http://feeds.cellphones.ca/~r/cellphonesetc/~3/7tirwysRljU/" target="_blank">Skype 3.0 for iPhone rolls out, Video-calling on iPhone now Live</a><br />');
document.write('<p>We <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0021024/\">heard it was coming</a>, at CES to be exact, but apparently, Skype didn?t want to wait that long and has just added video-calling functionality to the newest version of their iPhone app. </p> <p><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/Skype-3.0-iPhone-app-with-video-calling-.jpg\"><img src=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/Skype-3.0-iPhone-app-with-video-calling-.jpg\" alt=\"Skype 3.0 iPhone app with video-calling\" title=\"Skype 3.0 iPhone app with video-calling\" width=\"560\" height=\"411\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-21065\" /></a></p> <p>That?s right folks! Video-calling is now live on Skype 3.0 for the iPhone. What?s even better is, unlike FaceTime, this works on both WiFi and a 3G connection allowing you to enjoy video-calling virtually anywhere. Two-way video calling is supported on the <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/cell-phones/apple-iphone-4/\">iPhone 4</a> and <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/cell-phones/apple-iphone-3g-s/\">iPhone 3G S</a>, and can be viewed either in portrait or landscape mode. </p> <p>Skype 3.0 is compatible with the iPhone units running on as far back as iOS 3.0, but the video-calling feature only works with units installed with <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0015828/\">iOS 4.0</a> or later. Want to try it out? Head on over <a href=\"http://itunes.apple.com/us/app/skype/id304878510?mt=8\">here</a> to be redirected to the iTunes App Store to download this latest version of Skype for the iPhone. </p> <p>This is a post from <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/\">Cell Phones Etc.</a> entitled:<br /><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0021063/\">Skype 3.0 for iPhone rolls out, Video-calling on iPhone now Live</a></p><img src=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/cellphonesetc/~4/7tirwysRljU\" height=\"1\" width=\"1\"/>');
document.write('</li>');
document.write('<li class="rss-item"><a class="rss-item" href="http://feeds.cellphones.ca/~r/cellphonesetc/~3/-gtI4fyJyPA/" target="_blank">BlackBerry 6 upgrade for Curve 3G due in ?early January?</a><br />');
document.write('<p><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/08/BlackBerry-Curve-3G.jpg\"><img src=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/08/BlackBerry-Curve-3G-89x150.jpg\" alt=\"BlackBerry Curve 3G\" title=\"BlackBerry Curve 3G\" width=\"89\" height=\"150\" class=\"alignleft size-thumbnail wp-image-17179\" /></a>We know that a number of existing BlackBerry smartphones including the BlackBerry Curve 3G will be getting an appropriate BlackBerry 6 upgrade in due time, but since announcing their newest mobile platform version, RIM?s been pretty mum on its availability. Thankfully, carriers aren?t as secretive as the smartphone maker. Case and point, <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/cell-plans/carriers/telus/\">Telus</a> has just revealed over their <a href=\"http://twitter.com/TELUSsupport/statuses/20162498896338944\">Twitter Telus Support account</a> that the BlackBerry 6 upgrade for the <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/cell-phones/blackberry-9300/\">BlackBerry 9300</a> aka Curve 3G will begin to roll out in ?<em>early January.</em>? </p> <p>This was in response to an inquiry on when the BlackBerry 6 upgrade for the <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/cell-phones/blackberry-bold-9700/\">Bold 9700</a> will become available. Unfortunately, they didn?t have info on the Bold 9700 yet, but they were gracious enough to share what they know so far about the <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0016987/\">BlackBerry 6 upgrade</a>.</p> <p>Good news to end the year for Curve 3G owners. All we?re waiting for now is a specific release date. </p> <p>[<a href=\"http://mobilesyrup.com/2010/12/29/blackberry-6-upgrade-coming-to-the-telus-curve-3g-in-january/\">source</a>]</p> <p>This is a post from <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/\">Cell Phones Etc.</a> entitled:<br /><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0021057/\">BlackBerry 6 upgrade for Curve 3G due in &#8216;early January&#8217;</a></p><img src=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/cellphonesetc/~4/-gtI4fyJyPA\" height=\"1\" width=\"1\"/>');
document.write('</li>');
document.write('<li class="rss-item"><a class="rss-item" href="http://feeds.cellphones.ca/~r/cellphonesetc/~3/9ixDtRm_EB8/" target="_blank">New XPERIA phone gets leaked, Android 2.3 successor of the X10 Mini Pro?</a><br />');
document.write('<p>Still on the leak bandwagon, we now have one from the <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/cell-phones/manufacturers/sony-ericsson/\">Sony Ericsson</a> camp. There?s no name yet for this unofficial handset, but its purported to be the Android 2.3-flavored successor of the <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/cell-phones/sony-ericsson-x10-mini-pro/\">XPERIA X10 Mini Pro</a>. </p> <p><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/x10-mini-2-1.jpg\"><img src=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/x10-mini-2-1.jpg\" alt=\"x10 mini 2-1\" title=\"x10 mini 2-1\" width=\"270\" height=\"360\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-21055\" /></a> <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/X10-Mini-2.jpg\"><img src=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/X10-Mini-2.jpg\" alt=\"X10 Mini 2\" title=\"X10 Mini 2\" width=\"270\" height=\"360\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-21054\" /></a></p> <p>As far as specs go, this baby reportedly packs a 1GHz processor complemented by an Adreno 205 graphics chip, and a 3-inch 320&#215;480 LCD multitouch display. That&#8217;s not a lot to really get us excited for it, but thanks to these very telling photos, we now know that its does pretty well on Neocore (42.5fps) and ranks high using the Quadrant benchmark app (1,533). </p> <p>That?s all for now. However, given that <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0021000/\">MWC 2011</a> is all raring to go come February, we?re pretty sure we?ll be hearing more about this new XPERIA phone in the coming weeks. </p> <p>[<a href=\"http://translate.google.com/translate?js=n&#038;prev=_t&#038;hl=en&#038;ie=UTF-8&#038;layout=2&#038;eotf=1&#038;sl=zh-CN&#038;tl=en&#038;u=http://se.it168.com/thread-1838485-1-1.html\">source</a>]</p> <p>This is a post from <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/\">Cell Phones Etc.</a> entitled:<br /><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0021052/\">New XPERIA phone gets leaked, Android 2.3 successor of the X10 Mini Pro?</a></p><img src=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/cellphonesetc/~4/9ixDtRm_EB8\" height=\"1\" width=\"1\"/>');
document.write('</li>');
document.write('<li class="rss-item"><a class="rss-item" href="http://feeds.cellphones.ca/~r/cellphonesetc/~3/9AI3AWQSH3E/" target="_blank">Motorola Cliq 2 gets leaked, Hitting T-Mobile store on January 19?</a><br />');
document.write('<p>Meet the Motorola Cliq 2. It?s not official yet, but rumor is it?ll be launched at CES next month and will roll out by the 19th on <a href=\"http://cellphones.ca/cell-plans/carriers/t-mobile\">T-Mobile</a>. </p> <p><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/Motorola-Cliq-2.jpg\"><img src=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/Motorola-Cliq-2.jpg\" alt=\"Motorola Cliq 2\" title=\"Motorola Cliq 2\" width=\"560\" height=\"223\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-21050\" /></a></p> <p>So, what?s the Cliq 2 got to offer? It?s got a uniquely designed honeycomb-inspired QWERTY keypad, and also packs a 5-megapixel camera with LED flash, Bluetooth 2.1, Wifi (b/g/n), aGPS, and possibly HSPA+ connectivity as well. It?s still not clear though what Android OS it?ll come with, but safe to say, at the very least, we?re expecting this to come preloaded with Android 2.2 and will be Gingerbread-ready if it?s not yet installed with the latest version of Android. It?s will also reportedly come with a new version of MotoBLUR. </p> <p>That?s about it for now. Pricing is still a mystery. Rest assured though, once we get a hold of new info, we?ll be reporting it to you guys ASAP.</p> <p>[<a href=\"http://www.cellphonesignal.com/exclusive-this-is-the-new-motorola-cliq-2-another-android-phone-for-t-mobile/\">source</a>]</p> <p>This is a post from <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/\">Cell Phones Etc.</a> entitled:<br /><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0021048/\">Motorola Cliq 2 gets leaked, Hitting T-Mobile store on January 19?</a></p><img src=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/cellphonesetc/~4/9AI3AWQSH3E\" height=\"1\" width=\"1\"/>');
document.write('</li>');
document.write('<li class="rss-item"><a class="rss-item" href="http://feeds.cellphones.ca/~r/cellphonesetc/~3/zv8SfwA9kXQ/" target="_blank">Windows Marketplace: 5,000 apps and counting</a><br />');
document.write('<p>Still on the fence on whether to get a Windows Phone 7 handset or not? Is app availability a major concern for you? If so, then maybe this little bit of trivia will help you out. </p> <p><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/Windows-Marketplace-apps.jpg\"><img src=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/Windows-Marketplace-apps.jpg\" alt=\"Windows Marketplace apps\" title=\"Windows Marketplace apps\" width=\"560\" height=\"276\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-21045\" /></a></p> <p>Based on the latest tally of <a href=\"http://wp7applist.com/stats/\">WP7AppList</a>, Microsoft?s Windows Marketplace now has 5000 apps to offer 72% of which are paid (that&#8217;s 3,600 if you don&#8217;t want to do the math). Most of the paid apps are retailing for just $0.99 and approximately 500 apps selling at $1.99. Category-wise, no surprise here, games make up the majority of apps available for download. 22% are games with tools and entertainment apps in 2nd and 3rd place with 15% and 10% respectively.</p> <p>5,000 apps may not be much when compared to the giants like of the <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0017757/\">Apple App Store</a> and Android Market, but still, 5,000 is no small figure. It?s a pretty good start, and with a whole new year ahead of them, I?m sure their app metrics will still drastically improved as the months slowly go by. </p> <p>So, is 5,000 apps good enough for you or are you still waiting for them to hit the 1 million mark first before you buy your first Windows Phone 7 handset?</p> <p>This is a post from <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/\">Cell Phones Etc.</a> entitled:<br /><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0021043/\">Windows Marketplace: 5,000 apps and counting</a></p><img src=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/cellphonesetc/~4/zv8SfwA9kXQ\" height=\"1\" width=\"1\"/>');
document.write('</li>');
document.write('<li class="rss-item"><a class="rss-item" href="http://feeds.cellphones.ca/~r/cellphonesetc/~3/YyEcKaPYoDU/" target="_blank">Bada 1.2 upgrade for Samsung Wave due in early 2011</a><br />');
document.write('<p>Do you own a <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/cell-phones/samsung-s8500/\">Samsung Wave S8500</a>? If you?re one of those who got enticed to get Sammy?s first Bada offering, here?s some good news for you.</p> <p><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/Samsung-Wave-Bada.jpg\"><img src=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/upload/2010/12/Samsung-Wave-Bada.jpg\" alt=\"Samsung Wave Bada\" title=\"Samsung Wave Bada\" width=\"400\" height=\"247\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-21041\" /></a></p> <p>Samsung has just announced over <a href=\"http://twitter.com/samsungbada\">Twitter</a> that they?ll be rolling out a Bada 1.2 upgrade for the Wave. It?ll first be available in Europe during the early part of 2011 with hitting other countries sometime in Q1. </p> <p>Bada 1.2 features several UI changes, improved security, and T9 Trace input, Samsung?s Swype alternative. It all sounds pretty good, but what we?re more interested to find out is whether or not the very first Bada phone will be eligible for the newer <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0020930/\">Bada 2.0 </a>. </p> <p>The Samsung Wave is currently available on <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/cell-plans/carriers/rogers\">Rogers</a> and <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/cell-plans/carriers/bell/\">Bell</a>. We?ll have more on this Bada 1.2 upgrade once local availability gets announced.</p> <p>[<a href=\"http://www.gsmarena.com/samsung_s8500_wave_all_set_for_a_bada_12_update_early_next_year-news-2173.php\">source</a>]</p> <p>This is a post from <a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/\">Cell Phones Etc.</a> entitled:<br /><a href=\"http://www.cellphones.ca/news/post0021039/\">Bada 1.2 upgrade for Samsung Wave due in early 2011</a></p><img src=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/cellphonesetc/~4/YyEcKaPYoDU\" height=\"1\" width=\"1\"/>');
document.write('</li>');
